      "side": 1,
      "message": "I actually don\u0027t think the existence of a deferred canvas is relevant. The point is that if a recording doesn\u0027t have any knowledge that it was drawing to a deferred canvas, it should ignore any surface provided on replay rather than crashing if it gets such a surface. This is the scenario happening in the failing Chrome tests. (Though I suppose that really no client should be doing this so maybe we want to fix up whatever Chrome is doing rather than validating this client behavior with a unit test.)",
